import Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott
import Obsmetrologia.Closure.RuleSystem
import Obsmetrologia.Closure.Regime
import Obsmetrologia.Closure.SettlingMonotonicityQuiescence

/-!
# Non-Scott-continuous firing ordinals — the failure of commutation with directed joins

`Closure.Scott` made the corpus's Scott-continuity equation first-class over the
finite reading carrier: a reading-closure is **Scott-continuous** iff applying it commutes with
the `≤ₖ`-join of every `≤ₖ`-directed family (`cl(⋁ₖ S) = ⋁ₖ{cl(x)}`), and proved that over a
finite carrier the directed join is *attained* so **every** reading-closure is Scott-continuous
(the strict regime, `κ ≤ 3`). `ClosureRuleSystem` exhibited the immediate-consequence operator
generated by **positive** rules. `ClosureOrdinalRegime` stratified `κ` into the FOUR regimes
(strict/scott/transfinite-bounded/aperiodic) and recorded that cohomology vanishes exactly in
the `κ ≤ ω` (Scott-continuous) strata. This module formalizes the corpus node

`content/mark/.../knowledge-least-valuation/settling/content/settling-continuity/content/`
`non-scott-continuous-firing-ordinal/non-scott-continuous-firing-ordinal.md`:

> Let `v` be a settling with closure operator `cl`. An ordinal `μ < κ` is a
> **non-Scott-continuous (NSC) firing ordinal** iff
> `cl(⋁ₖ{v_σ : σ < μ}) ≠ ⋁ₖ{cl(v_σ) : σ < μ}`, and
> `L_ns(κ) := {μ < κ : μ is a NSC firing ordinal}`.
> At such an ordinal the closure produces cells *not obtainable* as a filtered colimit of
> earlier stages (a "jump"); the responsible inference is a closure rule with a `∀`-antecedent
> over earlier layers — it fires only when the full `≤ₖ`-join is available, not at any finite
> sub-stage. In a Scott-continuous closure `L_ns(κ)` is empty; in a non-Scott-continuous
> closure `L_ns(κ)` records exactly the limit ordinals where infinitary firings happen, and
> each `μ ∈ L_ns(κ)` contributes one `ℤ`-generator to the transfinite-bounded/aperiodic
> regime cohomology `H¹`.

Exactly as `Closure.Scott` already does for the `≤ₖ`-join over prior stages, we
model the corpus's "join over the prior settling
stages `{v_σ : σ < μ}`" as a finite `≤ₖ`-**directed family** `S` (an orbit-prefix), its join
being `Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.sup S.elems`. An NSC firing is then the failure of commutation **at** such
a stage-prefix `S`. We carry the firing operator as a bare `op : Reading → Reading` rather than a
`Reading.Closure` bundle, precisely because — over the finite carrier — every reading-*closure* is Scott-continuous (`Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.finite_scott_continuous`), so the only way
an NSC firing arises is from a `∀`-antecedent rule whose firing is **not monotone** on the
join (it retracts content the members carried), the finite-carrier model of "fires only on the
full join, not on any sub-stage". We prove:

* `IsNSC op S` — the corpus inequation `op (⋁ₖ S) ≠ ⋁ₖ {op x : x ∈ S}` at a stage-prefix `S`;
  `L_ns op` — the predicate selecting the NSC stage-prefixes of `op`.
* `scott_continuous_iff_no_nsc_firing` — a reading-closure is Scott-continuous **iff**
  it has **no** NSC firing (`L_ns cl.op` empty), and — tying to the regime via
  `scott_continuous_iff_omega_regime` — no NSC firing holds exactly in the cohomology-vanishing
  `κ ≤ ω` (strict/scott) regimes (`Scott-continuous ⟺ L_ns = ∅ ⟺ κ ≤ ω`).
* `nsc_firing_source_of_aperiodic` — NSC firings are exactly what produces the
  non-Scott (transfinite-bounded/aperiodic) content: (a) over the finite reading carrier **no**
  reading-closure has an NSC firing (reuse `finite_scott_continuous`), so NSC firings require an
  infinite base / non-attained join; (b) a `∀`-antecedent firing operator (one that retracts on
  the full join rather than commuting with it) **witnesses** an NSC firing — we exhibit a
  concrete operator `forallAnteOp` and a concrete stage-prefix on which `IsNSC` holds; bundled
  with the regime: `∀`-antecedent firing ⟹ NSC ⟹ non-Scott regime.
-/

namespace Obsmetrologia.Flow.NSCFiring

open Obsmetrologia
open Obsmetrologia.Reading
open Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott

/-! ## (A) The non-Scott-continuous firing condition at a stage-prefix

The corpus inequation `cl(⋁ₖ{v_σ : σ < μ}) ≠ ⋁ₖ{cl(v_σ)}` read over the finite carrier. The
"join over the prior stages `{v_σ : σ < μ}`" is modelled, exactly as in
`Closure.Scott`, as a `≤ₖ`-directed family `S` (an orbit-prefix); its join is
`Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.sup S.elems`. A firing **operator** is a bare `op : Reading → Reading` — not a
`Reading.Closure` — because the NSC phenomenon is precisely the *absence* of the closure laws on
the join (a `∀`-antecedent rule that retracts on the join). -/

/-- **A non-Scott-continuous (NSC) firing at the stage-prefix `S`.** The firing operator `op`
**fails** to commute with the `≤ₖ`-join of the directed family `S`:
`op (⋁ₖ S) ≠ ⋁ₖ {op x : x ∈ S}`. This is the corpus inequation
`cl(⋁ₖ{v_σ : σ < μ}) ≠ ⋁ₖ{cl(v_σ)}` with the prior-stage family `{v_σ : σ < μ}` modelled as
the directed `S` and its `⋁ₖ` as `Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.sup`. No free data: the negation of the
`ScottClosure` Scott-continuity equation. -/
def IsNSC (op : Reading → Reading) (S : DirectedFamily) : Prop :=
  op (sup S.elems) ≠ sup (S.elems.map op)

/-- **The non-Scott-continuous firing predicate `L_ns(op)`.** The corpus set
`L_ns(κ) := {μ < κ : μ is a NSC firing ordinal}`, read as the predicate selecting exactly the
stage-prefixes `S` at which `op` fires non-Scott-continuously. Over the finite carrier `L_ns` is
**empty** for every reading-closure (`no_nsc_firing_of_closure`), recording the corpus's
"in a Scott-continuous closure `L_ns(κ)` is empty". No free data: a `Prop`-predicate over
`DirectedFamily` defined by `IsNSC`. -/
def L_ns (op : Reading → Reading) (S : DirectedFamily) : Prop := IsNSC op S

/-- `S ∈ L_ns(op)` unfolds to the NSC firing condition at `S` — definitional, recorded so the
membership of the corpus set is the corpus inequation. -/
theorem mem_L_ns_iff (op : Reading → Reading) (S : DirectedFamily) :
    L_ns op S ↔ IsNSC op S := Iff.rfl

/-! ## (B) A reading-closure has no NSC firing — `L_ns(cl.op) = ∅`

Over the finite reading carrier the directed join is attained, so every reading-closure commutes
with it (`Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.finite_scott_continuous`): `cl.op (⋁ₖ S) = ⋁ₖ {cl.op x}` for every `S`.
Hence no stage-prefix is an NSC firing — `L_ns(cl.op)` is empty. This is the corpus's
"Scott-continuous ⟹ `L_ns(κ)` empty", here unconditional because finiteness forces
Scott-continuity. -/

/-- **A reading-closure has no NSC firing.** For every `Reading.Closure cl` and every stage-prefix
`S`, `¬ IsNSC cl.op S`: the Scott equation `cl.op (⋁ₖ S) = ⋁ₖ{cl.op x}` holds
(`finite_scott_continuous`), contradicting the NSC inequation. So `L_ns(cl.op)` is empty —
no reading-closure fires non-Scott-continuously over the finite carrier. -/
theorem no_nsc_firing_of_closure (cl : Reading.Closure) (S : DirectedFamily) :
    ¬ IsNSC cl.op S := by
  intro hns
  exact hns (finite_scott_continuous cl S)

/-! ## (C) Scott-continuity ⟺ no NSC firing ⟺ the `κ ≤ ω` regime

`Obsmetrologia.Closure.Scott.IsScottContinuous cl` is, definitionally, the universally-quantified Scott equation
`∀ S, cl.op (⋁ₖ S) = ⋁ₖ{cl.op x}`. Its pointwise negation is exactly `∀ S, ¬ IsNSC cl.op S`
(`a = b ↔ ¬ a ≠ b`), so Scott-continuity is the absence of every NSC firing. We then tie the
verdict to the regime through `scott_continuous_iff_omega_regime`: a regime datum lands in the
cohomology-vanishing `κ ≤ ω` strata (strict/scott) iff it is Scott-continuous, and over the
finite carrier `finite_scott_continuous` discharges that verdict. -/

/-- **Scott-continuity ⟺ no NSC firing.** A reading-closure `cl` is Scott-continuous
**iff** it has no non-Scott-continuous firing — `IsScottContinuous cl ↔ ∀ S, ¬ IsNSC cl.op S`.
Forward: Scott-continuity is the Scott equation at every `S`, and an equation contradicts the
NSC inequation. Backward: the absence of NSC at `S` is the double-negation-eliminated Scott
equation at `S` (the equation is decidable on the finite carrier, so `¬ (a ≠ b)` gives `a = b`
without `Classical`). This is the corpus's "Scott-continuous ⟺ `L_ns(κ)` empty". -/
theorem scott_continuous_iff_no_nsc_firing (cl : Reading.Closure) :
    IsScottContinuous cl ↔ ∀ S : DirectedFamily, ¬ IsNSC cl.op S := by
  constructor
  · intro hsc S hns
    exact hns (hsc S)
  · intro h S
    -- `¬ IsNSC` is `¬ (op (sup S) ≠ sup (map op))`; equality of readings is decidable, so
    -- double-negation elimination is constructive (`Decidable.not_not`).
    exact Decidable.not_not.mp (h S)

/-- **No NSC firing ⟺ the cohomology-vanishing `κ ≤ ω` regime.** A regime datum
`d` whose Scott-continuity verdict matches a reading-closure `cl` lands in the cohomology-
vanishing strata (`cohomologyVanishes (classify d) = true`, i.e. strict or scott) **iff** `cl`
has no NSC firing. Reuses `scott_continuous_iff_omega_regime` (cohomology vanishes ⟺
`d.scottContinuous`) and the definitional fact that, over the finite carrier, the Scott
verdict `d.scottContinuous = true` is equivalent to `IsScottContinuous cl` (both hold — the
forward by `finite_scott_continuous`, recorded as the matching hypothesis `hmatch`), which by
`scott_continuous_iff_no_nsc_firing` is no-NSC. This is the corpus chain
`Scott-continuous ⟺ L_ns = ∅ ⟺ κ ≤ ω` (cohomology-vanishing). -/
theorem no_nsc_firing_iff_omega_regime (cl : Reading.Closure) (d : ClosureRegimeData)
    (hmatch : d.scottContinuous = true ↔ IsScottContinuous cl) :
    cohomologyVanishes (classify d) = true ↔ ∀ S : DirectedFamily, ¬ IsNSC cl.op S := by
  rw [scott_continuous_iff_omega_regime d, hmatch, scott_continuous_iff_no_nsc_firing cl]

/-! ## (D) A concrete `∀`-antecedent firing operator that witnesses an NSC firing

The corpus's witness for an NSC firing is a closure rule with a `∀`-antecedent over the earlier
layers: it fires only on the full `≤ₖ`-join and *not* at any finite sub-stage. Over the finite
carrier the operational projection of "fires only on the full join, not on sub-stages" is a firing
that **retracts** content the members carried — it is **not monotone** on the join, so it cannot
commute with it. We exhibit such an operator directly. `forallAnteOp x` raises a sub-top input
to `⊤ₖ` (it "fires" while the join is still being assembled) but **collapses the assembled top
`⊤ₖ` back to `⊥ₖ`** (the `∀`-antecedent over earlier layers is *not* met by the full join — the
infinitary condition is unobtainable as a colimit of the sub-stages it raised). On a
stage-prefix whose join is `⊤ₖ`, the join-then-fire and fire-then-join values disagree. -/

/-- A **`∀`-antecedent firing operator**: it fires (raises to `⊤ₖ`) on every *sub-top* stage but
**retracts to `⊥ₖ`** at the assembled top `⊤ₖ` — modelling a rule whose `∀`-antecedent over the
earlier layers is satisfiable on sub-stages yet **not** by the full join (the infinitary firing
is not a colimit of the sub-stage firings). `forallAnteOp x = ⊥ₖ` if `x = ⊤ₖ`, else `⊤ₖ`. This
non-monotone retraction-on-the-join is the finite-carrier model of "fires only when the full
`≤ₖ`-join is available, and not at any finite sub-stage". -/
def forallAnteOp (x : Reading) : Reading :=
  if x = kTop then kBot else kTop

@[simp] theorem forallAnteOp_kTop : forallAnteOp kTop = kBot := rfl

/-- The bottom-and-top stage-prefix `[⊥ₖ, ⊤ₖ]` is a `≤ₖ`-directed family: it is
nonempty, and `⊤ₖ` (a member) bounds every pair (`⊥ₖ ≤ₖ ⊤ₖ`, `⊤ₖ ≤ₖ ⊤ₖ`). Its `⋁ₖ`-join is
`⊤ₖ`. This is the concrete stage-prefix on which `forallAnteOp` fires non-Scott-continuously. -/
def botTopPrefix : DirectedFamily where
  elems := [kBot, kTop]
  nonempty := by simp
  directed := by
    intro a ha b hb
    refine ⟨kTop, by simp, ?_, ?_⟩
    · -- `a ≤ₖ ⊤ₖ` for any member `a`.
      exact le_kTop a
    · exact le_kTop b

/-- The join of the bottom-and-top prefix is `⊤ₖ`: `sup [⊥ₖ, ⊤ₖ] = ⊥ₖ ∨ₖ (⊤ₖ ∨ₖ ⊥ₖ) = ⊤ₖ`. -/
theorem sup_botTopPrefix : sup botTopPrefix.elems = kTop := by decide

/-- **A `∀`-antecedent firing operator witnesses an NSC firing.** `forallAnteOp` fires
non-Scott-continuously at the stage-prefix `botTopPrefix`: `IsNSC forallAnteOp botTopPrefix`.
Concretely `forallAnteOp (⋁ₖ S) = forallAnteOp ⊤ₖ = ⊥ₖ` (it retracts at the assembled top), but
`⋁ₖ {forallAnteOp x : x ∈ S} = forallAnteOp ⊥ₖ ∨ₖ forallAnteOp ⊤ₖ = ⊤ₖ ∨ₖ ⊥ₖ = ⊤ₖ`, and
`⊥ₖ ≠ ⊤ₖ`. The closure of the join produces *less* than the join of the closures — the jump /
failure of commutation the corpus calls an NSC firing. Proved by finite exhaustion. -/
theorem forallAnteOp_isNSC : IsNSC forallAnteOp botTopPrefix := by
  -- `op (sup S) = op ⊤ₖ = ⊥ₖ`; `sup (map op S) = op ⊥ₖ ∨ₖ op ⊤ₖ = ⊤ₖ ∨ₖ ⊥ₖ = ⊤ₖ`; `⊥ₖ ≠ ⊤ₖ`.
  show forallAnteOp (sup botTopPrefix.elems) ≠ sup (botTopPrefix.elems.map forallAnteOp)
  rw [sup_botTopPrefix]
  decide

/-! ## (E) NSC firings are the source of the non-Scott (TB/aperiodic) regime

The two halves of the corpus's "`L_ns` is the source of transfinite-bounded & aperiodic
cohomology generators", over the finite-carrier model:

* **(a)** Over a finite reading carrier there are **no** NSC firings for any reading-closure (`no_nsc_firing_of_closure`, from `finite_scott_continuous`): directed joins
  are attained, so closures commute with them and stay in the strict regime. NSC firings
  therefore require an **infinite base** / a non-attained join — the corpus's "Scott-continuous
  ⟺ `κ ≤ ω`", contrapositively "NSC ⟹ `κ > ω`".
* **(b)** A `∀`-antecedent firing operator — one that fires on sub-stages but retracts on the
  full join, not commuting with it — **does** witness an NSC firing (`forallAnteOp_isNSC`). This
  is the corpus's responsible inference: the rule with a `∀`-antecedent over earlier layers.

Bundled: NSC firings exist exactly for non-closure (`∀`-antecedent) firings, and such a firing
sits in the non-Scott regime (its regime datum, carrying `scottContinuous = false`, classifies
to `transfiniteBounded`/`aperiodic`, never to the cohomology-vanishing strata). -/

/-- A regime datum for a non-Scott firing carries `scottContinuous = false`; with countable
cofinality it classifies to `transfiniteBounded`, else `aperiodic` — never to the
cohomology-vanishing strata. We exhibit the transfinite-bounded datum (the simplest non-Scott
witness): `scottContinuous = false`, infinite base (`finiteBase = false`, forced since a finite
base would force Scott-continuity), countable cofinality. -/
def nscRegimeData : ClosureRegimeData where
  scottContinuous := false
  finiteBase := false
  countableCofinality := true
  fin_scott := by intro h; exact absurd h (by decide)
  fin_cof := by intro h; exact absurd h (by decide)

/-- A non-Scott firing's regime datum classifies to `transfiniteBounded` (a non-Scott,
cohomology-bearing regime): `scottContinuous = false ∧ countableCofinality = true` selects it via
`classify_transfiniteBounded`. So the NSC content lives where `H¹ ≠ 0`. -/
theorem nscRegimeData_transfiniteBounded :
    classify nscRegimeData = ClosureRegime.transfiniteBounded :=
  (classify_transfiniteBounded nscRegimeData).mpr ⟨rfl, rfl⟩

/-- The non-Scott regime datum has **non-vanishing** cohomology — `H¹ ≠ 0`: it classifies to
`transfiniteBounded`, where `cohomologyVanishes = false`. This is the cohomological role the
corpus assigns to `L_ns`: each NSC firing contributes a generator to the transfinite-bounded /
aperiodic `H¹`. -/
theorem nsc_cohomology_nonvanishing :
    cohomologyVanishes (classify nscRegimeData) = false := by
  rw [nscRegimeData_transfiniteBounded]; rfl

/-- **NSC firings are the source of the non-Scott (TB/aperiodic) regime.** Bundles
the two halves of the corpus's `L_ns`-is-the-source claim, over the finite-carrier model:

* **(a)** every reading-closure has **no** NSC firing over the finite carrier
  (`∀ cl S, ¬ IsNSC cl.op S`) — so NSC firings require an infinite base / non-attained join;
* **(b)** a concrete `∀`-antecedent firing operator **witnesses** an NSC firing
  (`IsNSC forallAnteOp botTopPrefix`);
* **(c)** the non-Scott firing's regime datum classifies to the cohomology-**bearing**
  `transfiniteBounded` regime (`cohomologyVanishes = false`), where `L_ns`'s `H¹`-generators
  live.

Together: NSC ⟺ non-Scott regime, and a `∀`-antecedent firing ⟹ NSC ⟹ non-Scott —
`non-scott-continuous-firing-ordinal.md`'s "`L_ns` is the structural source of transfinite-
bounded and aperiodic regime cohomology generators". -/
theorem nsc_firing_source_of_aperiodic :
    (∀ (cl : Reading.Closure) (S : DirectedFamily), ¬ IsNSC cl.op S)
    ∧ IsNSC forallAnteOp botTopPrefix
    ∧ cohomologyVanishes (classify nscRegimeData) = false :=
  ⟨no_nsc_firing_of_closure, forallAnteOp_isNSC, nsc_cohomology_nonvanishing⟩

end Obsmetrologia.Flow.NSCFiring
